0 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Full-Time Biology Assistant / Associate Professor Full-Time Biology Assistant / Associate Professor DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia with undergraduate and graduate programs invites applicants for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor. The position requires teaching organismal biology classes, including human anatomy and physiology courses, at the baccalaureate level, scholarship and service responsibilities. Reporting to the Program Director and Division Chair, the position is an academic, campus- based appointment with the start date of January 2, 2027. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned Ph.D. in Biology preferred. College/university teaching experience and familiarity with electronic course development preferred Content area expertise: organismal biology, anatomy and physiology, ecology Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with University policy Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents Excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to build relationships and work cooperatively with all constituents. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Successful experience working with diverse student populations. Successful experience guiding undergraduate research projects. SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: To apply, please complete the Thomas University application at https://apply.appone.com/job/698d0328547b955a94fa0a29 ; send an email with the subject noting “Assistant Professor Organismal Biology” to Anna Benefield, Human Resources Administrator, at abenefield@thomasu.edu , and include: Cover letter addressing the qualifications sited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact: Dr. LeAnna Willison  lwillison@thomasu.edu For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
