 Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Assistant or Associate Professor of Education DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia with undergraduate and graduate programs invites applicants for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Education.  The specialization is open but should reflect one of the disciplines represented in the division. The position requires teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, both on-campus and online, as well as scholarship, and service responsibilities.  Reporting to the Division Chair, the position is a campus-based faculty appointment. Preferred start is January 2027 but an August 2027 start may be considered for exceptional candidates. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned doctorate in a discipline represented within the division. Minimum of three years of K-12 experience. Demonstrated experience with curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation. Expertise with both in-person and online instruction. Experience leading academic programs Experience supervising candidates in clinical experiences. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with University policy. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience in a formal academic leadership role (e.g. program director, department chair, etc.). Experience leading educator preparation program(s) with active PK-12 school partnerships. Comprehensive awareness of current issues facing PK-12 education. Experience managing programmatic accreditation. TO APPLY: Please follow the link provided: https://apply.appone.com/job/6a970ac3e44ee1285905e1fb Required documentation includes: Cover letter addressing the qualifications cited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact Dr. John Meis: jmeis@thomasu.edu . For questions regarding the submission of required documentation, please email Anna Benefield: abenefield@thomasu.edu Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
