uman Resource Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Woodlands Ribbon Cutting & Public Open House Homecoming Spirit Week Geeks vs. Guardians 5K Fun Run Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Chair of Division of Education Chair of Division of Education DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia invites applications for the position of Chair of the Division of Education.  The chair oversees and promotes the division’s academic programs, scholarship, service, and outreach. The chair provides strategic leadership, evaluation, and mentoring and professional development for faculty and staff within the division. The chair is responsible for leading the division and enhancing its relationships with other departments within the university and with local school districts, 2-year colleges, and community stakeholders.  This is an on-campus position located in Thomasville, Ga.  Preferred start is January 2027 but an August 2027 start may be considered for exceptional candidates. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned doctorate in Education, specialization open, with academic credentials sufficient to merit appointment at the rank of either Associate or Full Professor Demonstrated success managing programmatic accreditation Demonstrated success with program development and oversight, budget oversight, and program assessment Significant experience with and strong commitment to educator preparation programs Evidence of excellence in teaching and commitment to student success across undergraduate and graduate programs Demonstrated success in faculty development, including mentoring across career stages and supporting promotion and advancement Track record of successful collaboration and relationship building with school district and 2-year college partners and community stakeholders Expertise in online instruction and program development (Canvas is the preferred platform) PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: K-12 teaching experience Experience with Georgia Professional Standards Commission program approval processes Experience with Canvas LMS and Jenzabar CMS Experience fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and innovative academic programming Leadership in state, regional, or national professional organizations related to the division’s disciplines. TO APPLY: Please complete the application at the provided link: https://apply.appone.com/job/6a9709f3e44ee1285905e1f7 Required documentation includes: Cover letter addressing the qualifications cited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact Dr. John Meis: jmeis@thomasu.edu . For questions regarding the submission of application materials, please contact Anna Benefield, Director of Human Resources, at abenefield@thomasu.edu. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
