tation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Assistant/Associate Registrar Assistant/Associate Registrar DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia with undergraduate and graduate programs invites applicants for the position of Assistant/Associate Registrar.  The position requires working extensively with student data records, and the student life cycle from acceptance to graduation and reports to the Registrar. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Prior experience in a Registrar’s office Proficient with Microsoft Office suite Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills Proven ability to think strategically and prioritize multiple tasks effectively Strong analytical skills with attention to detail and accuracy Ability to work independently with minimal supervision or reminders to complete tasks. Adherence to professional ethics including confidentiality Punctual and industrious work habits PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Prior experience with Jenzabar, Canvas or other campus and learning management systems is preferred A Bachelor’s degree is strongly preferred, plus related experience in higher education. TO APPLY: Please follow the link provided here: https://apply.appone.com/job/6a7f8b10320f2e866be9e8ea Required documentation includes: Cover letter addressing the qualifications cited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this opening, please contact Kate Owens at kowens@thomasu.edu For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact