ducation Human Resource Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Veterans Resource Fair Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Resident Director for University Housing Resident Director for University Housing Job Summary: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia with undergraduate and graduate programs, invites applicants for the position of Resident Director for University Housing. This position reports directly to the Dean of Students, Director of Housing, or designee. The Resident Director (RD) oversees the daily operations of a university undergraduate residence community. This position is a twelve-month appointment. The RD implements and enforces policies and regulations on a community level and works with university administration in multiple aspects of Residence Life. Additionally, the RD must have the ability to work effectively with residents and Resident Assistants (RAs), providing them with guidance, feedback, and support when needed. This is a live-in position that requires the RD to live in one of the residence halls in their assigned community. Responsibilities/Duties Trains, supports, supervises, and evaluates all Resident Assistants in the assigned university residence community. Oversees community-wide programming for residents and staff and serves as a resource for the RAs in their programming for residents. Ensures that university policies and housing procedures are consistently enforced. Ensures compliance with local, State, and Federal regulations and laws. Monitors the conditions of the housing facilities, ensuring security, working facilities, and adequate amenities and reports issues to the Dean of Students, the Director of Housing, the Director of Facilities, or other relevant officer of the University. Communicates resident concerns to the Dean of Students, Director of Housing, or designee . Listens, documents, and addresses resident concerns within the RD’s scope. Handles crisis/conduct issues in accordance with university policy. Responds immediately to emergencies beyond the scope and ability of the RAs Responsible for damage assessment. Performs special projects or duties as assigned. Requirements/Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Experience with student life in higher education, particularly in the area of residence life. Strong organizational, administrative, and interpersonal skills. Strong time management skills. Strong knowledge and experience in programming for late adolescents. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Technological proficiency, particularly with Microsoft and Google suites. Must be able to clear a criminal background check. Must have independent transportation beyond the university shuttle. Supplemental Information: To Apply: Please complete the application at https://apply.appone.com/job/68d30739146d8a3eec56bfa2 and include: Cover letter addressing the qualifications listed above. Resume Names and contact information of three professional references. These may include previous employers, coaches, professors, etc. Do not use family members or friends as references. All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. Review of applications will begin immediately and will close when all positions are filled. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this position, please contact Mr. Scott Grubbs, Dean of Students, at sgrubbs@thomasu.edu . For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Ms. Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomsu.edu Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
