ment (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Veterans Resource Fair Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Peer Tutor Peer Tutor Learning Support at Thomas University Part-Time (Approximately 10 hours per week) Position Description Peer tutors work one-on-one and in group settings with students to help them develop subject area knowledge. Additionally, peer tutors support students’ academic achievement by reviewing and clarifying classroom instruction, assisting with the development of study skills, time management, and basic organization, which help students acquire new knowledge, apply previously learned information to new settings, and develop problem-solving skills.  They also serve as role models demonstrating strategies, attitudes, and behaviors of successful learnings. Basic Job Expectations: Peer tutors support student learning by scaffolding learning from specific course content and by fostering appropriate learning strategies. To be successful, peer tutors may consult with faculty for course resources, guidance, and direction in order to best support students. Tutors conduct regularly scheduled one-on-one and weekly study group sessions throughout the semester as needed through in-person drop-in sessions, scheduled Zoom conferences, and weekly in-person study group sessions. Required Qualifications: A GPA of 3.5 or higher in all course(s) and/or academic subject areas for which tutoring services will be offered and a cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher. Excellent written and oral communication skills Strong time management and organizational skills Passion for helping others. Satisfactory completion of Canvas training modules before first tutoring session, and the successful completion of the National Tutoring Association’s Basic Tutoring Certificate after completing 30 hours of tutoring in Learning Support. Be available to work 10 hours per week. Students must submit a Peer Tutor Application, a writing sample, one academic reference, and an unofficial transcript. Preferred Requirements : Federal Work-Study and VA Work-Study eligible students preferred. All Federal Work-Study and VA Work-Study applicants must meet the eligibility requirements for Federal Work-Study or VA Work-Study and complete the appropriate online application. Duties and Responsibilities: Attend all meetings and training sessions as scheduled and arrive promptly for all tutoring sessions and study group sessions. Adhere to all tutoring guidelines and best practices for ethical tutoring and academic integrity. Maintain clear records of each session using LibCal and LibRerference, including but not limited to weekly schedule, documenting each tutoring session, and providing follow-up information to the Director of Learning Support. Monitor SpringShare Chat during shifts. Assist students as they develop study skills, problem-solving skills, and self-editing skills. Preparing for tutoring sessions by reviewing course related information. Consult with a tutee’s instructors and/or advisor for advice, guidance, and direction in peer tutoring support for students. Conduct in-person or online tutoring sessions as scheduled. Conduct at least one in-person study group lasting one hour each week to be scheduled during the time the Learning Commons is open. Inform and/or consult with the Director of Learning Support if problems are encountered, or the need arises for assistance relating to a specific tutoring situation. Work cooperatively with Learning Support peer tutor staff to deliver a cohesive tutoring program and to respond in a professional manner to diverse student needs. Submit unofficial transcripts and self-evaluation to the Director of Learning Support at the end of each semester as part of your semester evaluation. Complete Self-evaluation with the Director of Learning Support at the end of each year or during your last semester with Learning Support. Evaluation Expectations Each Peer Tutor will complete the following evaluation process at the end of each semester: Submit unofficial transcriptions to the Director of Learning Support to ensure that the minimum GPA is maintained. Submission of Self-Evaluation form Meet with Director of Learning Support to establish goals for following semester. Supplemental Information To apply, please complete the application at https://apply.appone.com/job/67ddeeb19e29c73878205d1a . Contact Information For questions about this position, please contact Professor Robin DePaola, Director of Learning Support, at rdepaola@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
    },
