y and Special Education Human Resource Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Veterans Resource Fair Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Athletics and Student Life Student Work-Study Assistant Athletics and Student Life Student Work-Study Assistant Department: Athletics and Student Life Employment Type: Federal Work-Study / Student Employment Reports To: Athletic Director, Student Life Staff, or Assigned Supervisor Position Summary The Athletics and Student Life Student Work-Study Assistant will provide support for athletic events, Student Life activities, and other special events on campus. This position assists with the preparation, execution, and breakdown of events to help ensure a smooth and positive experience for participants, spectators, students, and staff. This position requires flexibility, as students may be scheduled to work evenings, nights, weekends, and special events based on the athletic and Student Life calendars. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities may include, but are not limited to: Assisting with the setup, execution, and breakdown of athletic events and Student Life activities. Providing game-day support for athletic events, including: Gatekeeping and ticket collection Scoreboard operations Game clock operations Assisting with event setup and cleanup Directing spectators and providing general customer service Assisting athletic staff with other game-day responsibilities as assigned Assisting with evening and special events organized through Student Life. Helping with the setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, equipment, decorations, and other event materials. Assisting with student engagement activities and special campus events. Providing a welcoming, professional, and positive experience for students, spectators, guests, and campus visitors. Following all Thomas University policies and procedures. Performing other duties as assigned. Work Schedule Work schedules will vary based on athletic contests, Student Life programming, and special events. Students must be available to work a flexible schedule, which may include: Evenings Nights Weekends Athletic events Special events and campus activities Hours will be scheduled in accordance with the student’s Federal Work-Study eligibility and departmental needs. Qualifications Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study or student employment through Thomas University. Must be currently enrolled as a student at Thomas University. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong communication and customer service skills. Dependable, responsible, and punctual. Ability to follow directions and complete assigned tasks. Ability to work in a fast-paced event environment. Previous experience with athletic events, scoreboards, game clocks, or event operations is preferred but not required. Physical Requirements The position may require the ability to stand and walk for extended periods, assist with event setup and breakdown, and lift or move light to moderate equipment and materials as needed. Additional Information This position provides students with the opportunity to gain hands-on experience in athletic event management, game operations, Student Life programming, customer service, and campus event coordination. Students may work across multiple areas depending on the needs of the University, including athletic competitions, Student Life events, and other special campus activities. Please complete the application at https://apply.appone.com/job/6a8da05de03e24e7bf1db952 . Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
