ce Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Veterans Resource Fair Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Director of Housing Director of Housing DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education in Thomasville, Georgia with undergraduate and graduate programs invites applicants for the position of Director of Thomas University Housing. The Director of Housing provides strategic leadership for and oversight of all aspects of Housing at Thomas University. This individual will work with university students, faculty, and staff to foster a vibrant campus environment that supports student development, well-being, and success. In addition, the Director will supervise Resident Directors, Resident Assistants, and provide leadership and direction for residential programming.  The position is a twelve-month appointment and reports to the Dean of Students.  If the candidate is properly credentialed in a discipline offered by the university, the Director may be accorded status as an administrator with faculty status and teach within an academic program. RESPONSIBILITIES: Works with the Dean of Students and other relevant stakeholders to create and implement a guiding vision for Thomas University Residence Life Hires, trains, assigns, supervises, and evaluates the Resident Directors and Resident Assistants Trains, supports, schedules, and supervises all Resident Directors and Resident Assistants.  Hosts at least one all RD/RA meeting per month for supervision and training purposes Schedules and oversees all required residential programming and safety efforts (Title IX, alcohol awareness, fire drills, etc.) Works with the Dean of Students to provide fiscal management and oversight for the department budget Ensures that Resident Life policies and procedures, rules, and regulations are current and enforced Oversees room and roommate selection and assignment processes Works collaboratively with the Office of Student Accounts, Facilities, and other relevant university entities Responsible for crisis and risk management as it relates to housing Oversee the student arrival and departure process Manages housing for summer camps and other events Keep current with “best practices” as they relate to housing Works with the Dean of Students and other university personnel to collect and analyze data relevant to Residence Life Works with the Dean of Students and other relevant stakeholders on data-driven continuous improvement within TU Residence Life Performs special projects and other duties as assigned REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree in education, business, or related field from an accredited institution Prior leadership experience in Student Life and/or Residence Life Commitment to supporting the needs of students Demonstrated ability to work with minimal supervision Demonstrate conflict resolution, de-escalation, and intervention skills Accuracy in reporting and attention to detail Strong leadership and supervisory skills PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in student affairs, education, business, or related field from an accredited institution Prior leadership experience in Student Life and/or Residence Life with specific experience administering a residence hall or residential community TO APPLY: Please follow the link https://apply.appone.com/job/699e1c1dba0b215dd6224de4 Required documentation includes: Cover letter addressing the qualifications cited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this opening, please contact Mr. Scott Grubbs at sgrubbs@thomasu.edu . For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
