ce Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Athletic Shop Books, Athletic Gear and more Bookstore Athletic Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Veterans Resource Fair Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Director of Nursing Director of Nursing DESCRIPTION: Thomas University, seeks an entrepreneurial Director of Nursing who will expand our undergraduate and graduate Nursing programs by driving program enrollment growth through recruitment efforts and strategic partnerships. The position requires teaching undergraduate and graduate nursing courses, scholarship and service responsibilities. Reporting to the Division Chair, the position is an academic, campus- based appointment to begin in August, 2027. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned doctoral degree in nursing or MSN and doctorate in related field Online teaching experience in BSN and/ or MSN programs preferred Content area expertise: nursing education and/ or nursing administration Experience in managing nursing accreditation requirements Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with university policy Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents Excellent written and oral communication skills PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Successful experience working with diverse student populations. Successful experience guiding graduate research projects. PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES : Expand strategic relationships with 2-year schools, healthcare facilities, and other local constituents Drive enrollment growth Oversee planning and implementation of curriculum and program outcomes and assessments Manage departmental budget Manage data and prepare documents for institutional reporting and where applicable, programmatic accreditation Maintain course rotations and deploy appropriate semester course schedules Coordinate selection and ordering of textbooks Manage clinical affiliate sites Review applications and recommend hiring of adjuncts Coordinate development and evaluation of all program faculty Coordinate with Advising to facilitate student entry, progression, and graduation Assist with recruiting efforts and where applicable review admissions applications SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: To apply, please complete the Thomas University application at https://apply.appone.com/job/6ae0c7d74c271104dec8bd57 ; send an email with the subject noting “Nursing Director” to Anna Benefield, Director of Human Resources, at abenefield@thomasu.edu , and include: Cover letter addressing the qualifications sited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact: Dr. Kim Cribb kcribb@thomasu.edu For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University is an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
