Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Assistant/ Associate Professor of Nursing Assistant/ Associate Professor of Nursing DESCRIPTION: Thomas University an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education with undergraduate and graduate programs in Thomasville, Georgia seeks applicants for its Nursing faculty position teaching in both the BSN and MSN programs. This position requires participation in campus-based activities on a monthly basis and regular engagement with local stakeholders. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned doctoral degree in nursing or MSN and doctorate in related field Online teaching experience in BSN and/ or MSN programs Content area expertise: community health, nursing administration and education Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with university policy Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents Excellent written and oral communication skills SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: To apply, please complete the Thomas University application at https://apply.appone.com/job/6ae0c57d3a3962d2974856ea ; send an email with the subject noting “Nursing Faculty” to Anna Benefield, Office of Human Resources abenefield@thomasu.edu , and include: Cover letter addressing the qualifications sited above. Curriculum vita Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of terminal degree (Official transcripts due upon hire) All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact: Dr. Kim Cribb kcribb@thomasu.edu. For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomasu.edu . Thomas University is committed to diversity. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
